4. Entry-Controlled vs Exit-Controlled Loops

Entry-Controlled Loop — while
The condition is checked before the loop body executes.

#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int number = 5;

    while (number < 5) {
        printf("This will not print.\n");
        number++;
    }

    return 0;
}
---------------
Exit-Controlled Loop — do-while
The condition is checked after the loop body executes.
this type of loop is executed atleast once even if the codition is false.
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int number = 5;

    do {
        printf("This prints once.\n");
        number++;
    } while (number < 5);

    return 0;
}
